{
  "accepted_answers": [
    "Arizona",
    "Santa Cruz County, Arizona",
    "near Sonoita, Arizona"
  ],
  "explanation": "The original sources provide specific geographic details about the location of Fort Buchanan. D1S1 states it was founded 'three miles southwest of present-day Sonoita in Santa Cruz County, Arizona,' directly supporting both 'near Sonoita, Arizona' and 'Santa Cruz County, Arizona.' D3S1 also confirms the location as being in Arizona. While D2S1 and D2S2 mention Nogales, Arizona in the context of the rediscovery of the ruins, this does not establish Nogales as the location of the fort itself. Therefore, 'Nogales, Arizona' is excluded as it refers to an associated event rather than the actual location of the fort. The proposed candidate 'three miles southwest of present-day Sonoita' is included as it is a direct quote from the source and adds specificity."
}
